# Okoye, Mighty and Adored: "Whenever that creature attacks the monarch this turn, it gains double strike and trample".
# Bot1 is the monarch from turn 1. On turn 3 Okoye (the counter's target) attacks Bot2, who is not the monarch: she gets her
# counter but no keywords. On turn 4 Bot2's Llanowar Elves connect and Bot2 becomes the monarch. On turn 5 Okoye (the target
# again) and a second creature, an Ornithopter, attack Bot2, now the monarch: only Okoye, the creature that got the counter,
# gains double strike and trample; the Ornithopter keeps just its flying.

[Bot1 Deck]
Forest
Sol Ring
Mox Emerald
Mox Pearl
Okoye, Mighty and Adored
Ornithopter
Forest x2
Forest x10

[Bot2 Deck]
Forest
Llanowar Elves
Forest x15

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Forest.Play
Bot1.Hand.Sol Ring.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Forest.Activate
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Hand.Mox Emerald.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Hand.Mox Pearl.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Emerald.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Pearl.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Sol Ring.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Okoye, Mighty and Adored.Cast
Bot1.Pass
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Forest.Play
Bot2.Battlefield.Forest.Activate
Bot2.Hand.Llanowar Elves.Cast
Bot2.Pass
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Hand.Ornithopter.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Target(Okoye, Mighty and Adored)
Bot1.Attack(Okoye, Mighty and Adored > Bot2)
[T3 Bot1.Main2]
? Monarch = Bot1
? Bot1.Battlefield.Okoye, Mighty and Adored.Counters.PlusOnePlusOne = 2
? Bot1.Battlefield.Okoye, Mighty and Adored.Keywords = (absent)
[T4 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Attack(Llanowar Elves > Bot1)
[T5 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Target(Okoye, Mighty and Adored)
Bot1.Attack(Okoye, Mighty and Adored > Bot2; Ornithopter > Bot2)
Bot1.Pass

[Expect]
Turn = 5
Monarch = Bot2
Bot1.Battlefield.Okoye, Mighty and Adored.Keywords = DoubleStrike; Trample
Bot1.Battlefield.Ornithopter.Keywords = Flying
